-- title:
--   Pinsketch decoder II: tabulated field arithmetic, the standard evaluation point and the syndrome polynomial
-- statement:
--   This bundle fixes the field data that the decoder reads from its environment, and the two derived objects that the read stage materialises.
--
--   For a field $F$ that is a $\mathbb{Z}_2$-algebra, a basis $b$ of $F$ over $\mathbb{Z}_2$ with $w$ coordinates, and an injective sequence $(\iota_0,\dots,\iota_{N-1})$ of nonzero elements of $F$, the standard decoding table `detStd t N b ι` is a list of word-sized natural numbers. Its first three entries carry the parameters $(t,w,N)$; the remaining blocks encode the multiplication, squaring, inversion, positivity and image tables on the basis coordinates, whose addresses are delimited by `detMulBase`, `detSqBase`, `detInvBase`, `detPosBase`, `detImgBase` and `detEnd`.
--
--   Two further objects are defined: `eSeq b y` turns a packed syndrome $y \in (\mathbb{Z}_2^{w})^{t}$ into the $t$ field elements it encodes, and `syndromePoly` is the polynomial whose coefficients are the field elements stored by the read stage. `payloadAt` and `payloadField` extract the payload bits of one coordinate block. These are the objects compared by the verifier and consumed by the key solver, so the algebraic content of the decoder never has to mention a memory address.
-- source:
--   arXiv:2611.11409, Section 2.2 (Pinsketch parameters and decoder) and Appendix C; Dodis, Ostrovsky, Reyzin, Smith, Fuzzy Extractors: How to Generate Strong Keys from Biometrics and Other Noisy Data, SIAM J. Comput. 38(1), 2008, Section 6.3

